    "No row in trades, exit_state, pause_state, chain_state or lp_baseline was added, changed or removed between the 17:33 checkpoint image and the 20:25 merged image, and the commit-by-commit WAL replay shows no row that existed only in between (1 distinct row state across all 40 commit points).",
    "The 40 WAL frames are all current-generation, each a single-page commit of page 1 (the database header) that only increments the file change counter (1029..1068); user_version stays 7. Reproduced on a temp DB: a process that opens the DB the way src/utils/db.ts does at import (journal_mode, synchronous, busy_timeout, user_version = 7) and exits without close() adds exactly one page-1 commit. So the live DB was opened 40 separate times between 17:33:56 and 20:25:58 local time on 2026-05-29; the bytes cannot say which program made the opens. The window is consistent with test runs during the Phase 21 close-out commits (18:13 to 20:28).",
    "The three literal matches are the LADYS token (trades 2 and 3) and the LADYS pair (lp_baseline 2), both public-historical (captured in test/fork/fixtures/realLaunches/eth-v2-tp.json). Their tx hashes match no test literal. The rows are consistent with the Phase 21 live capture round trip (buy 16:40:17, sell 17:11:03 local, before the checkpoint); not verified on-chain (no network in Phase 22). They are not attributed to tests.",
    "sqlite_sequence for trades is 3 in both images while only ids 2 and 3 exist: a trade with id 1 was created and deleted at some time before the 17:33 checkpoint. Its content is not recoverable (no residual hex strings remain in either file; secure_delete is off in this SQLite build, but a page rewrite can overwrite freed bytes). Its origin is unknown.",
    "Extraction limits: 17 test files generate addresses or hashes at runtime, so a row they wrote could not be matched by literal. In this window no row changed at all, so the limit hides nothing here; it matters only for rows already present before 17:33."
